t trusted-main transport failure in the Module-size gate; the gate made one GitHub fetch attempt and failed closed. Plan is to keep fail-closed for real drift but retry transient trusted-main fetch failures in-step, with tests parsing the real workflow shell.","timestamp":1789018443104575001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review PASS at 2026-09-10T05:18Z; claiming and starting TDD. RED target: workflow parity test must prove the Module-size gate retries trusted-main fetch before the existing fail-closed path.","timestamp":1789022396590056001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD evidence: RED test tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_module_size_gate_retries_trusted_main_fetch_before_failing_closed failed because the Module-size gate had a single git fetch and reached the fail-closed error path with no retry. GREEN adds a three-attempt, 2-second in-step retry around the explicit GitHub trusted-main fetch; final failure still exits 1. Targeted validation now passes: ruff check/format-check on tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py and the full file's 40 tests.","timestamp":1789022514947503001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"First full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 failed with two findings. One was a real local contract mismatch caused by the new retry warning text: tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline_lock_47e9.py still forbade any warning containing the module-size fetch text. Fixed that test to assert the final exhausted path is ::error:: plus exit 1, allowing bounded retry notices. The other was tests/interfaces/queries/test_session_log_visibility.py::test_ready_count_invariant_to_session_logs failing because an internal git commit timed out after 30s under heavy local load; rerunning that exact test on the same code passed. Targeted regression set now passes: test_ci_workflow_parity.py, test_complexity_baseline_lock_47e9.py, and the session-log test (50 passed). Rerunning full verify now.","timestamp":1789031739603813001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation validation evidence: RED pinned the CI flake class with tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_module_size_gate_retries_trusted_main_fetch_before_failing_closed, which failed before the workflow change because the Module-size gate fetched trusted main exactly once. GREEN adds a bounded 3-attempt, 2-second retry around only that fetch while preserving the final fail-closed error/exit path. Targeted regression set passed: tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py, tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline_lock_47e9.py, and tests/interfaces/queries/test_session_log_visibility.py::test_ready_count_invariant_to_session_logs => 50 passed. Full local verify passed with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 and GIT_CONFIG_* unset: 20175 passed, 88 skipped, 19 warnings in 6124.17s.","timestamp":1789038014587950001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed fix to Gerrit as change 2964 (commit 63c60a8dcad9c). Awaiting LLM-Review and Verified votes before submit.","timestamp":1789038340663403001}],"created_at":1788913865938358001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"60625cbc-4959-46d4-849c-5f8bc5919bb7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8ea3-3750-6772-4ac6"},{"link_uuid":"b5625e8b-149a-404b-b72d-5d8e97dd94d4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7a35-1f17-349f-4de7"}],"description":"## Context / RCA\nHapuku change 2852 had two Gerrit Verified failures on the same patchset revision that passed unchanged on retry. Failure evidence:\n\n- run 34281406317 ubuntu lanes failed in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41` because the test ran `git show c57057f41:.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` inside a shallow Gerrit patchset checkout where that historical commit was absent.\n- run 34282833154 macOS py3.13 failed the module-size gate with `could not fetch main to verify the module-size limit lock; failing closed`.\n\nThe first class has since been fixed on main by vendoring the historical c57057f41 workflow fixture. The remaining same-class trusted-main fetch defect was the module-size limit lock: a single transient GitHub fetch failure made Verified fail closed even though the absolute module-size cap still ran locally against the patchset tree.\n\n## Plan\n1. Preserve the fail-closed semantics for real module-size limit drift: if trusted main is fetched and `.github/module-size-limit.txt` differs, the gate must still fail.\n2. Make transient trusted-main transport failures deterministic by adding an in-step bounded retry loop to the existing Module-size gate fetch, using the same explicit GitHub URL and existing `refs/remotes/gh-main` destination. The final failed attempt remains fail-closed.\n3. Add RED coverage in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` that parses the real Module-size gate shell from `_build-and-test.yml` and proves it retries the trusted-main fetch before the existing fail-closed error path.\n4. Keep the existing vendored c57057f41 fixture contract as the regression guard for shallow-checkout historical workflow parity.\n5. Verify with targeted tests and full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2`, then land through Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41` no longer depends on the historical commit being present in the runner's shallow checkout.\n- [x] The Module-size gate retries transient trusted-main fetch failures before failing closed.\n- [x] The Module-size gate still fails closed if all trusted-main fetch attempts fail.\n- [x] The Module-size gate still fails when the fetched trusted-main limit differs from the patchset limit.\n- [x] The trusted-main fetch continues to use the explicit `https://github.com/${{ github.repository }}` URL, not an assumed `origin` remote.\n- [x] Targeted workflow-parity tests pass.\n- [x] `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before Gerrit review.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Make the Module-size gate trusted-main fetch retry transient transport failures while preserving final fail-closed semantics."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"Regression tests for shallow-checkout historical fixture use and module-size trusted-main fetch retries."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7a35-1f17-349f-4de7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e2da630b-5284-4c70-8f13-9b8408aa74f1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","infra"],"ticket_id":"47d0-8971-aa37-46fe","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit Verified retry needed after trusted-main fetch and ancestry failures","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f305ae34-c8b6-4178-af84-d3227bd714b3","c01b905a-193b-4713-9746-c3ac51dc637f","98945856-2e79-4445-a55e-1f73712ae478","ce7bb5e1-e4bb-47de-8006-672afaefa472","e2da630b-5284-4c70-8f13-9b8408aa74f1","0fbf1e6c-2357-4169-adf5-8948c50ede64","02a8c0c2-3555-4e1f-b983-c34715a6e956","7f47e36b-9371-44e3-9261-0d583db2a57c","675304f8-c9c3-42db-9839-32f1448bfcee","469cc310-f19a-418e-b5bc-bdead1456808","307c1a18-fdeb-452f-a51f-18471ae82275","095f8a26-dcb9-461e-8e86-85b863972595","b5625e8b-149a-404b-b72d-5d8e97dd94d4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789038611816372729,"uuid":"a22e3b48-2b04-4d83-81fa-160b0fb78958"}